Complete the graph by adding the Drama bar for $18$ students.
To which labelled value should its top reach?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.75]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,7.4); \draw[->] (0,0)--(5.5,0);
\foreach \y/\lab in {1/3,2/6,3/9,4/12,5/15,6/18} {\draw (-0.15,\y)--(0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,\y) {$\lab$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,0) {$0$}; \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (2,0) {Drama};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.3,3) {Students}; \node[below] at (2,-1.0) {Club}; \node at (2,7.1) {Club members};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The Art and Music bars are complete.
The Science count is $32$.
To which labelled value should its missing bar reach?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,6.4); \draw[->] (0,0)--(7.5,0);
\foreach \y/\lab in {1/8,2/16,3/24,4/32,5/40} {\draw (-0.15,\y)--(0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,\y) {$\lab$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,0) {$0$}; \draw (0.4,0) rectangle (1.6,3); \draw (2.4,0) rectangle (3.6,5);
\foreach \x/\lab in {1/Art,3/Music,5/Science} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {\lab};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.3,2.5) {Votes}; \node[below] at (3,-1.0) {Subject}; \node at (3,6.1) {Favourite subject};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A category has frequency $0$.
How should its bar appear on this graph?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.75]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.4); \draw[->] (0,0)--(5.5,0);
\foreach \y/\lab in {1/5,2/10,3/15,4/20} {\draw (-0.15,\y)--(0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,\y) {$\lab$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,0) {$0$}; \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (2,0) {Absent};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.3,2) {Students}; \node[below] at (2,-1.0) {Category}; \node at (2,5.1) {Attendance};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A student draws these bars for Group A: $24$ items, Group B: $48$ items and Group C: $36$ items.
One column height is incorrect. Which correction matches the supplied data?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.72]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.4); \draw[->] (0,0)--(7.5,0);
\foreach \y/\lab in {1/12,2/24,3/36,4/48} {\draw (-0.15,\y)--(0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,\y) {$\lab$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,0) {$0$}; \draw (0.4,0) rectangle (1.6,2); \draw (2.4,0) rectangle (3.6,3); \draw (4.4,0) rectangle (5.6,3);
\foreach \x/\lab in {1/A,3/B,5/C} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {\lab};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.3,2) {Items}; \node[below] at (3,-1.0) {Group}; \node at (3,5.1) {Group totals};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
